INT. LOCKER ROOM, COMMUNITY COLLEGE GYM - 5:40 A.M.

Gray light through frosted windows. Rows of dented lockers. A bench bolted to the floor. A shower drips somewhere, patient as a metronome.

DESHAWN PRITCHARD-AMADI (20s, lean, wrapped in a towel, hands taped to the wrist) sits on the bench, staring at his own feet. A gym bag rests between his ankles. A cheap phone sits on his knee.

He picks it up. Puts it down.

The PA system clicks overhead.

DESHAWN (V.O.)
(recorded, over PA)
All fighters report to the ring in fifteen minutes. All fighters, fifteen minutes.

He winces. Stops. Realizes his own recorded voice is the one on the PA, the one he left for the gym's morning announcements. He lets out a short laugh.

DESHAWN
Fifteen minutes.

He flexes his fingers inside the tape. Stands. Rolls his neck until it pops.

DESHAWN (CONT'D)
(to himself)
Not scared. Not scared.

He opens the locker, takes out a pair of worn red gloves, and holds them up to the light as if they might tell him something. They don't.

The shower drips. He slides the gloves on. Taps them together once, twice.

DESHAWN (CONT'D)
(louder)
Okay. Okay.

He walks to the mirror, looks himself in the eye, and does not look away.

DESHAWN (CONT'D)
Let's go.

The PA clicks again. His own voice returns, patient, indifferent.

DESHAWN (V.O.)
(recorded, over PA)
All fighters report to the ring.

He opens the door. The sound of a distant crowd rolls in like surf.
